def hiptensorContract(handle, plan, alpha, A, B, beta, C, D, workspace, workspaceSize, stream):
    r"""Performs tensor contraction :math:`D = \alpha \mathcal{A} \mathcal{B} + \beta \mathcal{C}`.

    Computes: :math:`\mathcal{D}_{{modes}_\mathcal{D}} \gets \alpha * \mathcal{A}_{{modes}_\mathcal{A}} B_{{modes}_\mathcal{B}} + \beta \mathcal{C}_{{modes}_\mathcal{C}}`.
    The active HIP device must match the device that was active during plan creation.

    Args:
        handle (:py:obj:`~.hiptensorHandle`/:py:obj:`~.object`) -- *IN*:
            Opaque handle representing the hipTensor library context.

        plan (:py:obj:`~.hiptensorPlan`/:py:obj:`~.object`) -- *IN*:
            Opaque handle containing the contraction execution plan.

        alpha (:py:obj:`~.rocm.bindings.util.types.Pointer`/:py:obj:`~.object`) -- *IN*:
            Scaling factor for :math:`A*B`. Data type determined by `descCompute`. Pointer to host memory.

        A (:py:obj:`~.rocm.bindings.util.types.Pointer`/:py:obj:`~.object`) -- *IN*:
            Pointer to tensor A data in GPU-accessible memory. Must not overlap with elements written to D.

        B (:py:obj:`~.rocm.bindings.util.types.Pointer`/:py:obj:`~.object`) -- *IN*:
            Pointer to tensor B data in GPU-accessible memory. Must not overlap with elements written to D.

        beta (:py:obj:`~.rocm.bindings.util.types.Pointer`/:py:obj:`~.object`) -- *IN*:
            Scaling factor for C. Data type determined by `descCompute`. Pointer to host memory.

        C (:py:obj:`~.rocm.bindings.util.types.Pointer`/:py:obj:`~.object`) -- *IN*:
            Pointer to tensor C data in GPU-accessible memory.

        D (:py:obj:`~.rocm.bindings.util.types.Pointer`/:py:obj:`~.object`) -- *OUT*:
            Pointer to tensor D data in GPU-accessible memory.

        workspace (:py:obj:`~.rocm.bindings.util.types.Pointer`/:py:obj:`~.object`) -- *OUT*:
            Optional parameter (can be `NULL`). Additional device memory workspace for optimizations.

        workspaceSize (:py:obj:`~.int`) -- *IN*:
            Size of the `workspace` array in bytes.

        stream (:py:obj:`~.rocm.bindings.util.types.Pointer`/:py:obj:`~.object`) -- *IN*:
            HIP stream for all computations.

    Returns:
        A :py:obj:`~.tuple` of size 1 that contains (in that order):

        * :py:obj:`~.hiptensorStatus_t`: One of:
                - :py:obj:`~.HIPTENSOR_STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED`: When the operation isn't supported.
                - :py:obj:`~.HIPTENSOR_STATUS_INVALID_VALUE`: When input data is invalid (typically user error).
                - :py:obj:`~.HIPTENSOR_STATUS_SUCCESS`: When the operation completes successfully.
                - :py:obj:`~.HIPTENSOR_STATUS_NOT_INITIALIZED`: When the handle isn't initialized.
                - :py:obj:`~.HIPTENSOR_STATUS_ARCH_MISMATCH`: When the plan was created for a different device than the currently active one.
                - :py:obj:`~.HIPTENSOR_STATUS_INSUFFICIENT_DRIVER`: When the driver is insufficient.

    .. rubric:: C signature

    .. code-block:: c

        hiptensorStatus_t hiptensorContract(const hiptensorHandle_t handle, const hiptensorPlan_t plan, const void * alpha, const void * A, const void * B, const void * beta, const void * C, void * D, void * workspace, uint64_t workspaceSize, hipStream_t stream)
    """
    ...

